---
// A CNAME chain: your name aliases a CDN's name, which has the addresses. The chain is only as
// fresh as its shortest TTL. Below, why the zone apex cannot be a CNAME.
---

<svg viewBox="0 0 400 372" width="100%" role="img" aria-labelledby="dns-cn-t dns-cn-d">
  <title id="dns-cn-t">Following a CNAME chain</title>
  <desc id="dns-cn-d">
    Three boxes from top to bottom. www.shop.example.in, in your zone, is a CNAME for
    shop.cdn.net, with a TTL of one hour. shop.cdn.net, in the CDN's zone, has two A records,
    192.0.2.80 and 192.0.2.81, with a TTL of 60 seconds. The resolver follows the chain and
    returns both records; the whole answer may be cached only for the shortest TTL, 60 seconds.
    At the bottom, a red box: example.in itself cannot be a CNAME, because the apex of a zone
    already holds SOA and NS records, and a CNAME may not share a name with any other record.
  </desc>
  <defs>
    <marker id="dns-cn-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
      <path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 z" style="fill: var(--viz-flow)" />
    </marker>
  </defs>

  <g font-size="19">
    <rect x="4" y="6" width="392" height="62" rx="8" stroke-width="2" style="fill: var(--viz-client-soft); stroke: var(--viz-client)" />
    <text x="16" y="32" font-weight="700" style="fill: var(--viz-ink)">www.shop.example.in.</text>
    <text x="16" y="56" font-size="17" style="fill: var(--viz-ink); font-family: var(--sl-font-mono)">CNAME shop.cdn.net.  TTL 3600</text>

    <line x1="200" y1="70" x2="200" y2="106" stroke-width="2" style="stroke: var(--viz-flow)" marker-end="url(#dns-cn-arrow)" />
    <text x="212" y="94" font-size="17" font-weight="600" style="fill: var(--viz-flow)">follow the alias</text>

    <rect x="4" y="112" width="392" height="88" rx="8" stroke-width="2" style="fill: var(--viz-server-soft); stroke: var(--viz-server)" />
    <text x="16" y="138" font-weight="700" style="fill: var(--viz-ink)">shop.cdn.net.</text>
    <text x="16" y="164" font-size="17" style="fill: var(--viz-ink); font-family: var(--sl-font-mono)">A 192.0.2.80  TTL 60</text>
    <text x="16" y="188" font-size="17" style="fill: var(--viz-ink); font-family: var(--sl-font-mono)">A 192.0.2.81  TTL 60</text>

    <text x="200" y="232" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="600" style="fill: var(--viz-ok)">cache the answer for 60 s,</text>
    <text x="200" y="256" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="600" style="fill: var(--viz-ok)">the shortest TTL in the chain</text>

    <rect x="4" y="276" width="392" height="90" rx="8" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="6 4" style="fill: var(--viz-bad-soft); stroke: var(--viz-bad)" />
    <text x="16" y="302" font-weight="700" style="fill: var(--viz-bad)">✗ example.in. CNAME …</text>
    <text x="16" y="328" font-size="17" style="fill: var(--viz-ink)">The apex already holds SOA and NS,</text>
    <text x="16" y="352" font-size="17" style="fill: var(--viz-ink)">and a CNAME can't share its name.</text>
  </g>
</svg>
